POWER BI DASHBOARD OUTLINE

PAGE 1 — OVERVIEW
•	KPI Cards:
o	Avg screen time
o	% exceeding limit
o	Total records
•	Screen time distribution (Histogram/Area chart)
•	Quick summary text (1–2 insights)
Purpose
•	To give a first impression of the problem severity

PAGE 2 — AGE-BASED ANALYSIS
•	Bar chart → Screen time by age group
•	Line chart → Trend of screen time across ages
•	% exceeding limit by age group
•	Apply slicers (Urban/Rural, Gender)
Purpose
•	To understand how screen usage changes with age
•	Identify critical age groups

PAGE 3 — DEVICE USAGE ANALYSIS
•	Donut chart → Device usage share
•	Bar chart → Screen time by device
•	Device usage across age groups
•	Filter by age group to see device preference changes
Purpose
•	To identify most used devices
•	Understand device impact on screen time

PAGE 4 — BEHAVIOR ANALYSIS (LIMIT & USAGE TYPE)
•	Column chart → % exceeding limit by age & gender
•	Stacked bar → Educational vs Recreational usage
•	Box plot → Screen time variation
Purpose
•	To analyze behavior patterns
•	To see if usage is productive or excessive

PAGE 5 — COMPARATIVE ANALYSIS (LOCATION & GROUPS)
•	Bar chart → Screen time by Urban vs Rural
•	Device usage by location
•	Gender-based comparison
•	Combine filters (e.g., Female + Rural + Teen)
Purpose
•	To compare different groups
•	Identify which group is more affected

PAGE 6 — ADVANCED INSIGHTS & SUMMARY
•	Heatmap → Age vs Device (cohort analysis)
•	Peak usage charts (by device, age, location)
•	Key insights (bullet points)
Final Section
•	Summary of findings:
o	High % exceeding limits
o	Increase with age
o	Smartphone dominance
o	Recreational usage higher
•	Early intervention (age-based control)
•	Device usage monitoring
•	Awareness on health impact
Purpose
•	To present final conclusions and actionable insights

